From bde93d10b4c2771324eb0e61b8c06d1f3a4df255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UZDoom NX2 <uzdoom-nx2@users.noreply.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:19:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] Switch 2 0.1.1: fixes from the first console test

- Vulkan failed to start with big mods ("out of device memory"): RDoom's
  object pool (a newlib workaround) took 128 KB-aligned slabs from
  libounce's small heap-page pool, which mimalloc needs for OunceVK's first
  32 MB segment. The pool and the malloc wraps are off on the Switch 2.
- Fatal errors were invisible: Vulkan still held the display layer.
  Switch_I_FatalError releases it before showing the error console.
- GPU lost in a level: RDoom's Switch 1 (Tegra X1) renderer workarounds
  default to UZDoom's own behaviour on the Switch 2 (NX_SW1_DEFAULT), and
  configs saved by 0.1.0 are migrated once (rd_defaults_rev 4).
- OunceVK's shader cache in switch/uzdoom-nx2/cache/ouncevk
  (MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR), cleared with the other shader caches.
- perf.log reports the heap's real use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
